# Documentation

Adapted from awesome-cursorrules how-to documentation + README practices.

## Prefer

- Task-oriented sections: prerequisites → commands → expected artifacts.
- Link normative contracts (`DATA_CONTRACT.md`, schemas, ADRs) instead of
  duplicating long tables.
- After Plan Mode, save the plan under `docs/plans/` (see `plan-mode-docs`
  rule) with decisions, schemas, and non-goals.
- Update `docs/TODO_PIPELINE.md` status only when acceptance criteria are met.
- Keep `docs/PROJECT_MAP.md` in sync when adding major packages or entrypoints.

## Avoid

- Marketing fluff; inventing CLI flags that are not implemented.
- Pasting huge raw inventories into docs—point at `reports/inspection/`.
